{
  "id": "u06-l03",
  "unit": "u06-bazaar",
  "title": "Please give me…",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Commands change with the same three levels of 'you'. For 'give':\n\n- **দে** (*de*) — তুই (close friends)\n- **দাও** (*dao*) — তুমি\n- **দেন** (*den*) — আপনি, everyday Bangladesh\n- **দিন** (*din*) — আপনি, standard (and the usual form in Kolkata)\n\n**দেন** and **দিন** are both correct and polite; this course accepts either. (দিন is also 'day'; context tells them apart.) There's no separate word for 'please' here: the polite verb form *is* the politeness. **আমাকে চা দিন** = 'Please give me tea.'\n\n**আমাকে** (*amake*) is 'me' as an object (compare **আমার** 'my'). **একটা** = 'one, a' (countable things); **একটু** = 'a little': **একটু পানি দাও**. **আরও** (*aro*) = 'more': **আরও একটু** 'a little more' (in speech **আর একটু** is common too).\n\n*Culture:* with a shopkeeper always use আপনি forms, even when you call him **মামা**: *মামা, একটা ডিম দেন।* Using দে with a stranger sounds rude.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "amake",
      "bn": "আমাকে",
      "tr": "amake",
      "en": "me",
      "notes": "Object form of আমি: আমাকে দেন 'give me'."
    },
    {
      "id": "den",
      "bn": "দেন",
      "tr": "den",
      "en": "give (polite)",
      "notes": "Polite imperative of দেওয়া 'give', used in everyday Bangladeshi speech. Also the present-tense 'you/he (polite) give'."
    },
    {
      "id": "din-give",
      "bn": "দিন",
      "tr": "din",
      "en": "give (polite, standard)",
      "notes": "Standard / more formal polite imperative. Same spelling as দিন 'day' — context tells them apart. Usual in Kolkata."
    },
    {
      "id": "dao",
      "bn": "দাও",
      "tr": "dao",
      "en": "give (familiar)",
      "notes": "Goes with তুমি."
    },
    {
      "id": "de",
      "bn": "দে",
      "tr": "de",
      "en": "give (intimate)",
      "notes": "Goes with তুই — only with close friends, younger siblings, small children."
    },
    {
      "id": "ektu",
      "bn": "একটু",
      "tr": "ektu",
      "en": "a little",
      "notes": "Also softens a request, like 'just': একটু দেন 'please give (me) a little'."
    },
    {
      "id": "aro",
      "bn": "আরও",
      "tr": "aro",
      "en": "more",
      "notes": "আরও = \"(even) more\"; don't confuse with আর \"and / else\". Also spelled আরো."
    }
  ],
